Block navigation to / rendering of the internal HTTP proxy path (AIKIDO-2026-728255)

The internal Capacitor HTTP proxy (CapacitorBridge.httpInterceptorStartIdentifier)
fetches an arbitrary remote URL and returns its body at the app origin. It is only
meant to be reached as an XHR/fetch subresource. If a (sub)frame navigates to the
proxy path, attacker-controlled content would render with full bridge access.

This backports the iOS portions of upstream commits 430356a9 and 80b6c5e8:
  * Only serve the proxy when CapacitorHttp is enabled; otherwise fail the scheme task.
  * Emit a "sandbox; frame-ancestors 'none'" CSP on proxied responses so nothing renders it.
  * Cancel any (main-frame or subframe) navigation to the proxy path in decidePolicyFor,
    before plugins get a chance to allow it.

